## Error Handling & Validation (merged)

* **Guard clauses**: check preconditions at the top of functions and return early with helpful errors.
* **Custom error types / factories**: define application-specific errors to unify handling and mapping to HTTP status codes.
* **Logging & telemetry**: always log unexpected errors with context, but avoid exposing internals to users.
* **User-friendly messages**: surface clear guidance in API error messages (e.g., `"email already registered"`).

---

## Performance & Scalability

* **Async for I/O**: convert all I/O boundaries (DB, networks) to async.
* **Caching**: use Redis for frequently accessed or heavy payloads; set TTLs and cache invalidation rules.
* **Lazy loading & pagination**: for large datasets, return cursors/pagination and lazily fetch data.
* **Serialization**: keep Pydantic models minimal; avoid returning giant objects when not necessary.

