## Commenting & Rationale policy (practical compromise)

* **Every production code line must have a short comment** explaining the *reason* that line exists (why this action is taken), not restating the obvious.
* **Length cap**: keep comments to one short sentence (≤ 12 words) where possible to avoid bloat.
* **Non-obvious logic**: expand into short multi-line block comments, still focused on rationale.
* **Docstrings**: each public function must include a one-paragraph docstring describing intent and RORO contract.

